{title: Holy God, We Praise Thy Name}
{artist: Ignaz Franz · tr. Clarence Walworth}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[F]Holy God, we [Bb]praise thy [C]name; [F]Lord of [Bb]all, we [C]bow be[F]fore thee!
All on earth thy [Bb]scepter [C]claim, [F]all in [Bb]heaven a[C]bove a[F]dore thee;
[C]infinite thy [F]vast do[C]main, [F]ever[Bb]last[C]ing [F]is thy reign.

Verse 2
[F]Hark! the [Bb]loud celestial [C]hymn [F]Angel [Bb]choirs above [C]are raising,
Cherubim and seraphim, [Bb]In [C]unceasing [F]chorus praising; [Bb]Fill the heavens
[C]with sweet [F]accord: Holy, [F]holy, holy, Lord.

Verse 3
[F]Lo! the apostolic [Bb]train Join [C]the [F]sacred Name to [Bb]hallow; Prophets [C]swell the loud
refrain, And the white [Bb]robed [C]martyrs [F]follow; And from [Bb]morn to set of
[C]sun, Through [F]the Church [F]the [F]song goes on.

Verse 4
[F]Holy Father, Holy [Bb]Son, Holy [C]Spirit, [F]Three [Bb]we name [C]Thee; While in
essence only One, Undivided [Bb]God [C]we [F]claim [Bb]Thee; And adoring bend
[C]the knee, [F]While we [F]own the mystery.
